From e63685e24bce6384a91e5b1c521e8ae46d390a95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:21:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Allow video sinks to request stored rasters and source pixel
 aspect

An unmarked anamorphic frame may contain views selected by a consumer-side hint or correction. Preserve its native samples on request before FFmpeg converts it, without manufacturing stereo metadata. Keep the existing default consumer path and make the sink request safe to read from the rendering thread.

The published +10 sink reproduction fails before this change. Native delivery passes afterward, the default consumer pixel hash is identical, and 43 buffer/property checks pass.

Assisted-by: gpt-6 (Codex)
